  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="section-why">
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="section-why">Why Improv Works For Teams</h2>
    <ul class="book-offer-list work-why">
      <li>
        <div>
          <strong>Listening to understand, not just reply</strong>
          <p>At work, people usually spend meetings planning what to say next while someone else is talking. In improv, planning ahead doesn't work. You have to listen to the last syllable before you know what comes next. That muscle carries straight back to the desk.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <strong>Saying "yes, and"</strong>
          <p>People learn to build on each other's ideas instead of instinctively shooting them down. Better, more collaborative conversations follow.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <strong>Lowering the stakes</strong>
          <p>A room where it's safe to look silly and make mistakes is a room where people feel safe taking creative risks the rest of the year.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

